{"term":"roar","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d0f1dede438efe1f07","definition":"To make a loud, deep cry, especially from pain, anger, or other strong emotion.","example":"Sole on the barren ſands the ſuff'ring chief / Roar'd out for anguiſh, and indulg'd his grief.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["uproar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:81cba229bc1b4259ae","definition":"To laugh in a particularly loud manner.","example":"The audience roared at his jokes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uproar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:42c3a1e5e5d64a36ae","definition":"Of animals (especially a lion), to make a loud deep noise.","example":"The lioness roared to scare off the hyenas.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uproar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8fadf6e7e9f13f37bc","definition":"Generally, of inanimate objects etc., to make a loud resounding noise.","example":"The brazen throat of war had ceased to roar.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["uproar"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roar#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:967ad2eabb76820177","definition":"To proceed vigorously.","example":"United's attempt to extend t